00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:42.791
It looks like 2019 is going to be an awesome
year for Stephen King fans with Pet Sematary

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.180
and IT: Chapter 2 on the way; and if you followed
my channel in 2017, you’ll know IT was one

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.480
of the first big Things You Missed episodes to
get super popular.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.530
So today we’ll be taking a drive down the
road from Derry, Maine to Ludlow, Maine to

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.500
take a look at all the Things You Missed in
the new trailer for Pet Sematary.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.640
Roll it.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.480
“So many trees.”

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.660
“It’s beautiful right?”

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.280
“It’s definitely not Boston.”

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.120
That’s right, it looks like the Creed family
moves to Maine from Boston in this movie,

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.280
as opposed to Chicago, where they’re from
in the book.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.220
Chicago is also where the parents of the wife,
Rachel Creed, live.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.820
There’s further evidence in the family’s
Massachusetts license plate, and Louis’s

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.590
Cape Cop shirt, which also has the year 2016
printed on it, signaling that the 2019 version

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:28.200
will be at, or near present day, just like
IT: Chapter 2 which will be set in 2016.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.560
The time period may also hold a clue as to
why the family is now from Boston instead

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.560
of Chicago.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.740
In the book, which takes place in the 80s,
there’s a scene where Rachel needs to quickly

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.190
get back home while visiting her parents in
Chicago.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:41.130
She ends up booking a series of connecting
flights, and there’s even a scene in the

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.229
1989 movie where she runs through the terminal
to board a flight that has already closed

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:46.229
its doors.

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:49.920
In a post-9/11 setting however, none of that
is as realistic, so the family may be located

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.680
out of Boston so that Maine is just a drive
away, rather than a flight away.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.400
Boston’s Logan International Airport is
 the closest airport to Maine that Rachel

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.380
is able to get to in the book, and she ends
up driving from there to her home, so making

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.220
the family from Boston in this movie just
simplifies that journey.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.780
Hear that cry in the background?

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.739
That’s the cry of the Wendigo, a mythological
cryptid said to be located in the Northeastern

00:02:14.739 --> 00:02:15.739
United States.

00:02:15.739 --> 00:02:19.590
The Wendigo is one of the better known Native
American legends, said to be a human cannibal

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:24.629
transformed over time into a giant bipedal
deerlike creature that eats human flesh.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:29.400
In Pet Sematary the book, the Wendigo cursed
the Micmac tribe burial ground in Ludlow,

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.940
granting it the power to bring those who are
buried their back to life as undead cannibals.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.840
We don’t actually get to see the Wendigo
in the 1989 movie, but there may be a clue

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:43.370
in the 2019 trailer that it will make an appearance
this time -- I’ll get back to that later

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.769
on in this video.

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:49.030
So the drums played by the animal mask children
represent the tribal music of the Micmac tribe,

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.769
and the cry heard in the distance could be
the Wendigo.

00:02:51.769 --> 00:02:55.400
Speaking of the kids in the animal masks,
what’s the deal with them?

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.530
As far as I can remember, there are no such
kids in the book, so who are they?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:04.029
In the book, there are a couple of old stories
told by the Dr. Creed’s neighbor, Jud Crandall.

00:03:04.029 --> 00:03:07.269
When he first shows them the Pet Sematary,
he explains that it was created by kids who

00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:12.150
had lost their pets to trucks on the dangerous
road the town is situated on.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:17.049
My guess is that this is just a flashback
scene showing the kids burial ritual for their

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:18.049
pets.

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:21.150
The trailer is cut to make it look like Rachel
and Ellie actually see the kids’ funeral

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.799
procession, but I don’t think the actual
movie will be cut like that; just speculating

00:03:24.799 --> 00:03:26.650
here, but I think they’re just using clips
out of context.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.700
We also get to see the family’s cat, Church,
who doesn’t look as creepy as the cat in

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:35.420
the 1989 version, but bears a much stronger resemblance
to his appearance on the cover of the book.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:39.360
There is a pretty creepy moment from the cat
though and we’ll talk about it later in

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:40.840
this video.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.830
As I mentioned, the road outside of the house
is extremely menacing.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:48.219
This shot of a truck blazing though seems
to be an exact replica of a shot used in the

00:03:48.219 --> 00:03:49.409
1989 movie.

00:03:49.409 --> 00:03:51.809
However, there is one noticeable difference.

00:03:51.809 --> 00:03:56.590
The license plate of this truck reads C61
-- the alphanumeric translation of which says

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.109
CGI.

00:03:58.109 --> 00:04:01.949
Maybe this is a small hint that this 2019
film will take advantage of computer generated

00:04:01.949 --> 00:04:06.840
imagery to do things that the 1989 version
wasn’t able to, like show a realistic rendering

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:10.799
of the Wendigo, or show a more graphic depiction
of “the scene”.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.120
(Those of you familiar with the story know
the one I’m talking about.)

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.940
But, for all I know, maybe this is just a
set of random letters and numbers, let me know

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.900
what you think in the comments.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.389
The next thing I’d like to point out is
the scene here of Louis getting out of bed

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:27.720
and discovering that his feet are covered
in dirt.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.440
In the book, this takes place right after
he has this dream, where the ghost of one

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.599
of his former patients, most likely this guy,
brings him to the Pet Sematary and warns him

00:04:35.599 --> 00:04:40.501
never to cross this barrier, known as the
Deadwood, the divide between the Pet Sematary

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:42.820
and the cursed burial ground.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.220
He wakes up at first relieved that it was
just a dream, until his daughter notices the

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.440
smell and he discovers his feet are covered
in dirt.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.530
Louis’s deceased patient, Victor Pascow,
makes several appearances to Rachel in the

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.900
80s movie adaptation, and that looks to also
be the case in 2019.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.990
Remember when I first talked about the first
trailer for IT, and pointed out that Pennywise’s

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.389
eyes were, at the time, missing from the reflection
in the water?

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:11.720
"If you look closely at Pennywise's reflection
right here, you'll notice that it's eyes don't

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.300
seem to reflect in the water.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.800
Which is pretty creepy if you ask me."

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:16.800
Yeah.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.110
Get a load of this.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.259
Hopefully they don’t end up replacing the
eyes for the final movie, like they did for

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:24.830
IT, unless it ends up being even creepier
than the dark void.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:29.540
One thing that was absent from the 1989 movie
adaptation is a character named Norma Crandall,

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:34.100
Jud’s old arthritic wife who, in the book,
without spoiling anything, is a central part

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.140
in setting the main events in motion.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:40.080
She’s replaced by this caretaker character
named Missy Dandridge in the 80s movie, but

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.460
this quick shot in the trailer could possibly
mean that she’ll have an appearance in the

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.860
upcoming film.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.560
Side note -- the reason that I keep referring
to it as “an upcoming movie” is because

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:51.880
I always get these comments on my movie trailer
Things You Missed episodes that say, “this

00:05:51.889 --> 00:05:55.379
is so stupid, analysing the trailer, why don’t
you just watch the movie?”

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:59.220
Which I do almost always put out a longer
Things You Missed for the movie as soon as

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.530
it’s out, but for whatever reason, there’s
always that person who ignores that episode

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.689
and comes to complain about the trailer analysis.

00:06:04.689 --> 00:06:09.110
So to those people watching after April 2019:
why don’t you just watch the episode that

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:11.090
I did on the movie?

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:14.770
The last thing I’d like to talk about though
from the trailer, is this image of the tree

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:15.900
with the spiral on it.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:19.210
This is another symbol that I don’t remember
being in the first movie, but it definitely

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:20.210
is in the book.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:23.620
Louis draws this shape in the dirt at one
of the graves with his finger without even

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.320
realizing he is doing so.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.349
Then, upon returning to the Micmac burial
ground, he realizes the entire thing is shaped

00:06:29.349 --> 00:06:33.169
like a spiral and wonders if anyone had ever
seen this land from above.

00:06:33.169 --> 00:06:37.870
So the spiral is a symbol of the power that
this cursed land has over the town and its

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:38.870
inhabitants.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.870
Continuing on with the analogy to IT, just
as Derry seems to have an overlooked history

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:47.090
of bad things happening to it that is driven
by the malevolence of Pennywise; Ludlow has

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.960
a similar force presiding over it driven by
the power of the Wendigo.

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.770
In other words, the spiral is to Pet Sematary
what the red balloon is to IT.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:59.479
If you’re looking forward to seeing Pet
Sematary, then leave a like on this video.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.740
Some of you may recall that the 89’ film
ended with an original song by The Ramones.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.420
"I don't want to be buried.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.660
In a Pet Sematary."

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:13.660
I highly doubt that there would be another
song tie-in today, but if there was, what

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.740
modern punk band do you think would perform
it?

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:19.509
I imagine it would probably be Fall Out Boy
or something, although there is a certain

00:07:19.509 --> 00:07:22.509
other band rumored to be returning in 2019…

00:07:22.509 --> 00:07:24.350
Let me know your thoughts in the comments.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:29.229
I’ll be covering a bunch of topics related
to the new adaptations of Pet Sematary and

00:07:29.229 --> 00:07:33.930
IT, so if you love Stephen King novels then
remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:39.389
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for
notifications and I’ll see you in the next

00:07:39.389 --> 00:07:40.389
one.

00:07:40.389 --> 00:07:42.729
Assuming we both survive.

